Purpose: Default the browser theme seed to Corvid's brand color (#5B6BC0) so the native toolbar and tabs take Material-3 tonal colors; no new UI.
Area: ui
Files: chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc (default of the kUserColor pref)
Rebase risk: low
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)
Status: BUILT and checked on 155.0.8059.39 (2026-10-14): a fresh profile under Xvfb shows a lavender tab strip and toolbar and an indigo omnibox focus ring (screenshot), no crash. Baseline in ThemeService means "no user color", so a profile that sets the color to transparent (reset to classic theme) gets the stock look. Not checked: dark mode, other platforms.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc b/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc
index cb1dd91e6d83..70bcd75bb131 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc
@@ -320,7 +320,11 @@ void ThemeService::RegisterProfilePrefs(
   registry->RegisterIntegerPref(
       prefs::kDeprecatedUserColorDoNotUse, SK_ColorTRANSPARENT,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
-  registry->RegisterIntegerPref(prefs::kUserColor, SK_ColorTRANSPARENT);
+  // Browser patch: the default theme seed is the browser's brand color
+  // (#5B6BC0) instead of "no color". Baseline means "no user color", so the
+  // native toolbar and tabs now take tonal colors from this seed until the
+  // user picks another color or resets to the classic theme.
+  registry->RegisterIntegerPref(prefs::kUserColor, SkColorSetRGB(0x5B, 0x6B, 0xC0));
   registry->RegisterIntegerPref(
       prefs::kDeprecatedBrowserColorVariantDoNotUse,
       static_cast<int>(ui::mojom::BrowserColorVariant::kSystem),
